Module hhg "The House That Grows" {
  Description "The causeway to Lowmere, and a red door on its pond arc.".

  Place causeway "the crater causeway" is room within causeway_country at 0, 0.
  Place pond_arc "Lowmere's pond arc" is room within lowmere at 1, 1.
  Place sennu_house "the house with the red door" is building within lowmere.
  Place sennu_kitchen "a cord-weaver's kitchen" is room within sennu_house at 1, 2.
  Passage west_road "the west causeway" is causeway between rim and causeway taking 2 hours.
  Passage lowmere_road "the causeway into Lowmere" is causeway between causeway and pond_arc taking 2 hours.
  Passage red_door "the red door" is door between pond_arc and sennu_kitchen.

  Observe causeway_scene at causeway as fixture when true "The causeway runs along crater-rims from town to town, a raised road of packed earth between ponds. Out on the plain, cribs of timber packed with wool-bale run in a fan toward the middle of the country: Lowmere's net, to catch the city.".
  Observe arc_scene at pond_arc as fixture when true "Lowmere is bigger than Cobble Ring: nine arcs of houses facing a wide pond, and every yard full of cord-weaving. On the pond arc one door is painted red.".
  Observe kitchen_scene_l at sennu_kitchen as fixture when true "A cord-weaver's kitchen, cord on every peg, and a loom by the window onto the pond.".

  Person sennu "Sennu Arru" at sennu_kitchen {
    Role "a cord-weaver of Lowmere, who sold her boy up to the city in the famine year". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Initially Assert kin(sennu, quill).
  Topic sennu_son with sennu "Ask Sennu Arru about the red door" when not cameHome(quill) {
    Says "'My husband painted it,' says Sennu, 'so the boy would know it from the sky.' She does not stop weaving. 'He was five. The famine year. They took him up as a Netter, for the tax.' The shuttle goes back and forth. 'They told us they'd call him something else.'".
  }
  Event quill_home near sennu when cameHome(quill) "Ottie stands in the red doorway and does not come in. Sennu looks up from the loom, and the shuttle falls out of her hand and runs across the floor on its thread. She says a name that is not Ottie. He says, 'You sang.'" then {
    Assert reunited(quill).
  }
  Relation reunited(group).
  Observe quill_stays at sennu_kitchen as ambience when reunited(quill) and at(quill, sennu_kitchen) "Ottie sits by the loom winding cord for his mother, very badly, and she lets him.".

  // Lowmere's net: the cribs on the plain, and the woman who walks them at first light.
  Person ketu "Ketu Sorrell" at pond_arc {
    Role "keeper of Lowmere's crib-line, who walks the wool-bale cribs at dawn to see what the city dropped". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Buys ithren_lamp for 2 coin.
    Buys dreg for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic ketu_net with ketu "Ask Ketu Sorrell what the cribs have caught" when true once {
    Says "'Wool, mostly, that the wind took off the city's washing-lines,' says Ketu. 'A pot. A pair of boots, once, with a man's feet gone out of them a long time since. And lamps.' She holds up her palm, flat, for the size of a pear. 'Dead as stones. The Company's clerk gives two marks apiece, and so do I, and the difference is that I do not write it on a slate.' She watches the sky the way other people watch a road. 'Nothing living, in my time. My mother's time, a girl. She said she walked home.'".
  }
  Topic ketu_boy with ketu "Ask Ketu Sorrell whether the cribs ever catch children" when not cameHome(quill) once {
    Says "'The cribs are for wool,' says Ketu, too quickly. 'Sennu Arru asks me that every first light, and every first light I tell her.' She is looking at the red door. 'They do not let them fall. They put them down. There is a hatch, Sennu says, and a rope. If you know the knot on the rope you know the child went up and not down.' She turns away to her cribs. 'Ask her about the knot. Not me.'".
  }
  Topic sennu_knot with sennu "Ask Sennu Arru about the knot on the rope" when not cameHome(quill) and knows(actor, knot_custom) once {
    Says "The shuttle stops, for the first time since you came in. 'The Netters' knot,' says Sennu. 'Tied like a fist, sealed with tar. My husband saw it once, on the rope they let down for the tax-man's barrel.' She puts her palm flat on the cord on the loom as if it were a face. 'You have seen where it goes.'".
  }
  Topic sennu_after with sennu "Ask Sennu Arru how the boy is" when reunited(quill) once {
    Says "'Bad at it,' says Sennu, with enormous satisfaction. 'The winding. The knot. He pulls it the Netters' way and I have to take it out.' She will not look at the door, which is open, which is how a house with a red door says it has stopped waiting. 'He asks what the nights are for. He says up there he was told they were for being counted.' The shuttle goes across. 'I told him they were for the other thing.'".
  }
  Observe red_door_open at pond_arc as ambience when reunited(quill) "The red door of the house on the pond arc stands open in the daytime, which neighbours have noticed: nobody has seen it open in the daytime since the famine year.".

  Place offstage "elsewhere" is site within strewnfield at 3, 3.
  Place nowhere "nowhere" is room within offstage at 0, 0.
}
